        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Both reagents are bases. A few drops remove H⁺ from the water ligands and give an uncharged hydroxide precipitate."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "label": "Precipitation with hydroxide ions",
          "formula": "[Cu(H₂O)₆]²⁺ + 2OH⁻ → Cu(OH)₂(H₂O)₄ + 2H₂O",
          "where": [
            "The simpler form Cu²⁺(aq) + 2OH⁻(aq) → Cu(OH)₂(s) is also accepted.",
            "With ammonia, NH₃ acts as the base: it takes H⁺ from the ligand to form NH₄⁺."
          ]
        },
